  "question": {
    "text": "Suppose that<br />Box-I contains <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn></math>&nbsp;red, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math> blue and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> green balls,<br />Box-ll contains <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>24</mn></math> red, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn></math> blue and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn></math> green balls,<br />Box-III contains <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> blue, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn></math> green and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math> yellow balls,<br />Box-IV contains <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math> green, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn></math> orange and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math> white balls.<br />A ball is chosen randomly from Box-l; call this ball <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi></math> is red then a ball is chosen randomly from Box-ll, if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi></math> is blue then a ball is chosen randomly from Box-III, and if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi></math> is green then a ball is chosen randomly from Box-IV. The conditional probability of the event &#39;one of the chosen balls is white&#39; given that the event &#39;at least one of the chosen balls is green&#39; has happened, is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
